# ==============================================================================
# Solar Store Management System - Environment Configuration Overview
# ==============================================================================
# This workspace follows a 3-tier architecture:
#   1. Local Development (Localhost, Docker Postgres / Supabase CLI)
#   2. Staging / Preview (Isolated Staging Supabase + Preview Host / Vercel)
#   3. Production (Isolated Production Supabase + Live Host / Vercel)
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Backend and Frontend have dedicated configuration files:
#     - Backend:  backend/.env.example, backend/.env.staging.example, backend/.env.production.example
#     - Frontend: frontend/.env.example, frontend/.env.staging.example, frontend/.env.production.example
# - Staging and Production databases MUST be completely isolated (different Supabase projects).
# - NEVER commit any active .env / .env.local / .env.staging / .env.production files.
# ==============================================================================

# Common Environment Reference Matrix
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKEND:
#   DATABASE_URL                 - Pooled Postgres connection (port 6543)
#   DIRECT_URL                   - Direct Postgres connection (port 5432, for migrations)
#   SUPABASE_URL                 - Supabase project URL (e.g. https://<ref>.supabase.co)
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY    - Admin service role key (Backend server only!)
#   SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET          - Supabase JWT secret (or omit if JWKS is used)
#   APP_URL                      - Frontend URL where invite / password reset links land
#   JWT_SECRET                   - Secret for signing receipt QR codes & internal tokens
#   CRON_SECRET                  - Secret for authorizing scheduled Vercel Cron endpoints
#   CORS_ORIGINS                 - Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins
#   BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN        - Vercel Blob storage access token (for cloud file uploads)
#   SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, ...    - Outbound email server credentials
#
# FRONTEND:
#   API_URL                      - Backend API host (proxied via /api rewrites)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL     - Supabase project URL (compiled into client bundle)
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY- Supabase anon/publishable key (compiled into client bundle)
